From: ACK72 <acikom72@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:56:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: share and recycle IPv6 source MAC slots safely

Isolate IPv6 flow source MACs from registered GDM base slots and KEEP.
Share live slots by reference count, reuse idle slots only after checked
hardware invalidation, and quarantine uncertain writes or deletions.
Serialize UPDMEM writes and preserve flow ownership when hardware entries
age, move or are reused. Exhaustion falls back to software forwarding.

Consolidates ACK72 patches 0024, 0026.

Adapted-from: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott@hotmail.com>, patches 972 and 973
Source: https://github.com/Gilly1970/Gemtek-W1700K-6.18/tree/4b8fb8c3a2619dd239fb44fd511ee2848a07e768/openwrt-patches
Adapted-from: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott@hotmail.com>, patch 973
Source: https://github.com/Gilly1970/Gemtek-W1700K-6.18/blob/4b8fb8c3a2619dd239fb44fd511ee2848a07e768/openwrt-patches/973-net-airoha-UPDMEM-slot-allocator-for-IPv6-source-MACs.patch

